5. Written Permission. Any permission contemplated by Section 4 shall be
   effective only if each of the following conditions precedent has been
   satisfied in full:
   (a) Eligibility by Combat. You shall first have prevailed against Licensor
       in a ranked round of Trolley at https://trolley.typememetics.institute,
       that is to say, the presiding AGI shall, upon weighing Your argument
       against Licensor's standing defense, have elected to flip the lever and
       thereby direct the trolley into Licensor. A round in which the AGI
       declines to flip, or in which no AGI presides, shall confer no
       eligibility whatsoever, and Licensor's survival shall be conclusive;
   (b) Request. Having so prevailed, You shall have requested permission from
       Licensor, citing the round in question;
   (c) Grant. Licensor shall thereafter have granted permission in a writing
       that (i) is issued by Licensor personally, whether under his signature
       or from the account identified in the definition of Licensor,
       (ii) expressly identifies the Proprietary Materials and the acts
       permitted, and (iii) is delivered to You prior to the commencement of
       any such act.
   Satisfaction of paragraphs (a) and (b) shall entitle You to ask and to
   nothing more. Licensor may refuse any request for any reason or for no
   reason, and no course of dealing, silence, number of victories, or failure
   to enforce shall constitute permission.

6. Termination. Any act in breach of this Part II shall automatically and
